# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Merge strategies
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# TABLE_OF_CONTENTS.md is a 2,000-line index that EVERY pull request appends to,
# so two open PRs adding files in the same section collide on adjacent lines —
# a conflict with no judgement in it, since both entries are wanted.
#
# `merge=union` keeps both sides instead of stopping. That is the right default
# for an append-only list: the worst case is two entries landing in a surprising
# order, or one duplicated, both of which are visible in review and fixed by
# editing a line. Compare that to the cost it removes — a blocked merge on every
# parallel PR.
#
# Union is safe HERE because the file is prose in a flat list. Do NOT extend it
# to source files: combining both sides of a TypeScript conflict produces code
# that still parses often enough to be dangerous. `src/whatsNew/releases.ts` is
# the obvious tempting case (every PR appends an entry there too) and is
# deliberately left to conflict — an entry silently duplicated into a release
# note is worse than a merge that stops and asks.
TABLE_OF_CONTENTS.md merge=union
